---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import framework from "../../content/framework/draft.json";
import "../styles/traditions-entry.css";
---
<BaseLayout fullBleed mainClass="homepage" description="Explore and compare political-economic systems, institutions, cases, and evidence.">
  <header class="traditions-hero">
    <p class="coordinate">ENDS AND MEANS / SYSTEMS IN THEORY AND PRACTICE</p>
    <div class="traditions-hero__thesis">
      <h1>Follow the claim<br /><span>from purpose to practice.</span></h1>
      <p class="dek">Explore what an approach values, the institutions it proposes, what happened in bounded cases, and which judgments the evidence can—or cannot—support.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="traditions-hero__guide" aria-label="How to use this guide">
      <p class="coordinate">FIRST CANONICAL SLICE</p>
      <p>The new graph is deliberately starting with one deeply traced example. It is a design and method test, not a claim that this subject deserves permanent priority.</p>
      <a href="/explore/swedish-wage-earner-fund-program/">Open the reviewed slice <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <section class="canonical-launch" aria-labelledby="canonical-launch-title">
    <header><p class="coordinate">EXPLORE / COMPARE / VERIFY</p><h2 id="canonical-launch-title">One graph, three ways into the argument</h2></header>
    <div>
      <article><p class="coordinate">01 / EXPLORE</p><h3>Swedish wage-earner fund program</h3><p>Trace attributed Ends through proposed Means, bounded implementation, Challenges, and Criteria.</p><a href="/explore/swedish-wage-earner-fund-program/">Explore the Approach →</a></article>
      <article><p class="coordinate">02 / CASE</p><h3>Enacted funds, 1984–1991</h3><p>Keep formal design, rules-in-use, outcomes, and interpretation visibly separate.</p><a href="/cases/swedish-wage-earner-funds/">Inspect the Case →</a></article>
      <article><p class="coordinate">03 / COMPARE</p><h3>Promise and practice</h3><p>Compare the same canonical Statements without manufacturing a score or duplicating prose.</p><a href="/compare/">Open Compare →</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tradition-catalogue legacy-catalogue" aria-labelledby="tradition-catalogue-title">
    <header class="tradition-catalogue__heading">
      <div>
        <p class="coordinate">TRANSITIONAL RESEARCH / {framework.traditions.length} DOSSIERS</p>
        <h2 id="tradition-catalogue-title">Earlier working material</h2>
      </div>
      <p>These dossiers remain available for provenance and feedback, but they have not yet been reconciled into the canonical graph.</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="tradition-cards">
      {framework.traditions.map((tradition) => (
        <li>
          <article class="tradition-card">
            <header>
              <p class="tradition-card__kind">Working dossier</p>
              <h3><a href={`/traditions/${tradition.id}/`}>{tradition.name}</a></h3>
            </header>
            <p class="tradition-card__summary">{tradition.overview[0]}</p>
            <div class="tradition-card__boundary">
              <span>Keep in view</span>
              <p>{tradition.distinctions[0]}</p>
            </div>
            <footer>
              <span>Transitional</span>
              <a href={`/traditions/${tradition.id}/`} aria-label={`Open the transitional ${tradition.name} dossier`}>View working material <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
            </footer>
          </article>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="secondary-discovery" aria-labelledby="archive-title">
    <header>
      <p class="coordinate">WORK IN PROGRESS</p>
      <h2 id="archive-title">The catalogue will grow after the structure survives review.</h2>
      <p>Gender, anarchism, historical transitions, people, and fictional Depictions are in the roadmap. We are testing the evidence path before multiplying pages.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="secondary-discovery__paths">
      <article>
        <p class="coordinate">METHOD</p><h3>How the graph works</h3><p>See why Concepts, Approaches, Means, Cases, Statements, and Sources remain distinct.</p><a href="/framework/">Read the method <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="coordinate">PROVENANCE</p><h3>Earlier questions and sources</h3><p>Browse the transitional research directory while canonical migration continues.</p><a href="/reading/">Inspect the reading directory <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
